1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:03,084
Here's how a preorder moves from the menu to the kitchen.

2
00:00:05,640 --> 00:00:07,082
Let's start with the menu.

3
00:00:07,107 --> 00:00:10,017
Customers can see prices and portions, then add a meal.

4
00:00:10,042 --> 00:00:12,365
They can review their basket before signing in.

5
00:00:17,360 --> 00:00:21,053
At checkout, customers enter their name and phone number, then create a

6
00:00:21,078 --> 00:00:21,362
passkey.

7
00:00:21,387 --> 00:00:24,460
They don't need a separate website password or email address.

8
00:00:29,480 --> 00:00:30,625
Want some ideas?

9
00:00:30,650 --> 00:00:32,964
Choose a date, quantity and budget.

10
00:00:32,989 --> 00:00:36,473
The finder suggests complete options, including one menu repeated.

11
00:00:36,498 --> 00:00:39,202
Customers can compare the choices before ordering.

12
00:00:43,280 --> 00:00:47,096
At checkout, choose an offered date, a morning time and the delivery

13
00:00:47,121 --> 00:00:47,416
area.

14
00:00:47,441 --> 00:00:50,617
The total is confirmed before the kitchen's receiving QR appears.

15
00:00:50,642 --> 00:00:52,537
A sample receipt is uploaded here.

16
00:00:52,562 --> 00:00:55,098
The kitchen still needs to verify the payment.

17
00:00:55,123 --> 00:00:57,979
The saved order is then shown in My orders.

18
00:01:06,800 --> 00:01:10,310
The kitchen can open the order and review its payment evidence.

19
00:01:10,335 --> 00:01:14,167
Recording payment and confirming that the food was received are separate actions.

20
00:01:16,960 --> 00:01:19,181
Stock updates when the order is placed.

21
00:01:19,206 --> 00:01:23,032
In this example, chicken goes from five thousand to four thousand eight

22
00:01:23,057 --> 00:01:24,316
hundred and seventy grams.

23
00:01:24,341 --> 00:01:26,241
One salad bowl is also deducted.

24
00:01:30,600 --> 00:01:34,762
For unlabelled ingredients, the owner can record shelf life and its reference.

25
00:01:34,787 --> 00:01:37,553
Earlier limits and held batches affect usable stock.

26
00:01:37,578 --> 00:01:41,042
These dates help with planning; they don't guarantee food safety.

27
00:01:44,440 --> 00:01:48,273
Finally, the kitchen can review the day's orders and print the matching

28
00:01:48,298 --> 00:01:48,916
slips together.

29
00:01:48,941 --> 00:01:52,130
Sales and costs follow their recorded payment and receipt rules.

30
00:01:52,155 --> 00:01:54,702
The order stays connected to the kitchen's records.
